    "created_at": "2025-09-25T12:36:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-25T12:38:14Z",
    "body": "https://drafts.csswg.org/css-align/#place-self-property - this doesn't have the dialog value defined, which is where I looked initially fwiw.\r\n\r\nI guess it being patched by the anchor positioning spec is *okay*?\r\n\r\nFwiw I'm not a massive fan of the 'dialog' value naming given popovers are explicitly *not* dialogs, but I also can't think of anything that's necessarily better.\r\n\r\nI'm guessing the computed values are all the same except for obviously these new values for place-self and justify-self? In which case the only \"breaking change\" here would be that stuff is actually aligned as expected in any realistic scenario.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/3333732423/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
