    "created_at": "2025-09-26T23:31:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-26T23:31:29Z",
    "body": "@annevk All right, bugs filed and tests merged. Should be good to go now.\r\n\r\n@lukewarlow \r\n> I guess it being patched by the anchor positioning spec is okay?\r\n\r\nYeah, the Anchor Pos spec also adds the 'anchor-center' alignment value. This isn't an unusual thing for CSS specs to do; neither of the values can do anything unless you've implemented Anchor Positioning anyway.\r\n\r\n> Fwiw I'm not a massive fan of the 'dialog' value naming given popovers are explicitly not dialogs, but I also can't think of anything that's necessarily better.\r\n\r\nThe WG also isn't particularly happy with the name, but we can't come up with anything better.\r\n\r\n>  In which case the only \"breaking change\" here would be that stuff is actually aligned as expected in any realistic scenario.\r\n\r\nIf you're somehow depending on the margin/etc being set how the previous UA stylesheet did (`margin:auto`, `width:fit-content`, etc), that could potentially mess you up; that's the most possible breaking change.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
